From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: let the external shell take comctl32 from beside its executable

Purpose: keep the XP shell on XP's comctl32 v6.
XP behavior: explorer's manifest redirects comctl32 to the v6 assembly,
and the loader applies that redirection before KnownDlls.
Wine before: since Wine 11, wineboot publishes KnownDlls and the DLLs
they import, so comctl32 (imported by comdlg32 and shell32) is a known
DLL and always comes from system32. The XP shell, which runs without its
SxS activation context and relies on the v6 copy beside xp-explorer.exe
instead, got XP's v5 comctl32: the desktop's icon labels got an opaque
background, the Start panel's right column, the taskbar buttons and the
folder window's menu bar were missing, and Win+E opened the desktop.
Change: with the opt-in, do not take comctl32.dll from KnownDlls; the
normal search order finds the copy in the application directory first.
Other known DLLs and processes without the opt-in are unchanged.
Evidence: +loaddll in the test VM shows C:\xp\comctl32.dll again, as
with Wine 10.0, and the shell's scenes match the Wine 10.0 build.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL, and only comctl32.dll.
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index c5c3493..5c32fb1 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 
 #include "wine/exception.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
+#include "wine/win4wine.h"
 #include "wine/list.h"
 #include "ntdll_misc.h"
 #include "ddk/ntddk.h"
@@ -3290,7 +3291,10 @@ static NTSTATUS find_dll_file( const WCHAR *load_path, const WCHAR *libname, UNI
                 TRACE( "Skipping file search for %s.\n", debugstr_w(libname) );
                 return STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND;
             }
-            if (!open_known_dll( libname, nt_name, pwm, mapping, image_info, id )) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+            /* The XP shell's comctl32 v6 lives beside its executable and stands in
+             * for the SxS redirection, which Windows applies before KnownDlls. */
+            if (!(win4wine_external_shell() && !wcsicmp( libname, L"comctl32.dll" )) &&
+                !open_known_dll( libname, nt_name, pwm, mapping, image_info, id )) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
         }
     }
 
